<title>THAILAND: Bank of Thailand seeks stability before rate cuts.</title>
<headline>Bank of Thailand seeks stability before rate cuts.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Thailand said on Monday that it would wait for a few months for clearer signs of economic stability before easing high Thai interest rates.</p>
<p>Assistant central bank governor Siri Ganjarerndee told reporters that Thai lending rates should not decline before the government sees more visible economic stabilising results after its recent 1996/1997 fiscal budget cuts.</p>
</text>
